# A bare ESP32-S3 on a board of its own, with its TRS port hanging straight off two pins (build.sh s3direct):
#  - TRS TIP on the S3's GPIO14, the data out in the default Type A
#  - TRS RING on the S3's GPIO15, held high in board_init() as Type A's current source
#  - TRS IN on the S3's GPIO21, through the 6N137
# Each of the two output pins has a 22 ohm resistor in series.
# The module is an ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 (16 MB flash, 8 MB OPI PSRAM). The 4 MB partition layout stays on
# purpose: it is frozen for OTA and shared with the other boards, and the image does not need the extra flash.
# PSRAM (octal) comes from sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, which already selects CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT.
# The console is TinyUSB's serial port on the native USB, as sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3 sets it (CONSOLE_NONE):
# USB-Serial-JTAG and TinyUSB share the PHY, and anything written to USB-Serial-JTAG after TinyUSB starts hangs
# the chip. There is no USB-UART bridge on the board.
CONFIG_AIRMIDI_BOARD_DIRECT_S3=y
